            <ArticleTitle>Benign multicystic peritoneal mesothelioma associated with hydronephrosis and colovesical fistula formation: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>808-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mesotheliomas usually arise from the pleura and are malignant. We report an unusual case of benign peritoneal mesothelioma presenting in a 59-year-old woman. The disease resulted in bilateral hydronephrosis, colovesical fistula formation, recurrent small bowel obstruction and chronic abdominal pain. To date only a handful of cases have been reported and to the best of our knowledge, none has been so aggressive.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
